Description: CARLOS EMR - Canadian electronic medical record (single-host deployment)
 CARLOS (Clinical Assisting Recording Ledger Open Source) is an open-source
 electronic medical record for Canadian primary care, with HL7 and FHIR
 interfaces and Ontario and British Columbia billing support.
 .
 This package deploys the whole system on one machine: the CARLOS web
 application on a dedicated Tomcat 11 instance, a MariaDB schema provisioned
 with least-privilege accounts, and an nginx front door running ModSecurity 3
 with the OWASP Core Rule Set in blocking mode. TLS is on by default with a
 self-signed certificate that can be replaced by a certbot-managed Let's
 Encrypt certificate at any time. Nightly restic backups and a weekly restore
 drill are installed as systemd timers.
 .
 Every long-running component is unprivileged: the application runs as the
 system user "carlos", backups as "carlos-backup", nginx as "www-data" and
 MariaDB as "mysql". Root is used only by the package maintainer scripts and
 by the certificate-renewal timer.
 .
 For a container-based, multi-pod deployment with an observability stack see
 the carlos-podman project instead.

